==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-cross the line.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[overstep]] a [[boundary]], [[rule]], or [[limit]]; to [[go too far]] or do something unacceptable.
#: {{syn|en|go too far|overstep the mark}}
#: {{ux|en|I can tolerate a lot, but they really '''crossed the line''' when they broke the equipment.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2020|artist=Pet Shop Boys|album=Hotspot|title=Monkey Business|passage=Bring me margaritas, champagne and red wine / We're gonna have a party / Where we all '''cross the line'''}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/oct/05/climate-activists-insulate-britain-roadblocks-kit-malthouse|title=Climate activists crossed the line with roadblocks, says minister|date=2021-10-05|author=Damien Gayle|quotee=Kit Malthouse|work=The Guardian|passage=Climate change protesters “'''crossed the line'''” between their right to protest and their responsibility towards the rest of the public when they caused huge tailbacks by blocking three key London roads on Monday, the policing minister, Kit Malthouse, has said.}}
# To finish a race.
#: {{syn|en|go all the way}}
#: {{ant|en|fall at the last hurdle}}
# To achieve completion of something.
#: {{syn|en|go all the way}}
#: {{ant|en|fall at the last hurdle}}
# To cross the [[equator]], as a [[vessel]] at [[sea]].<ref>{{R:Webster 1913|line}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|cinematography}} To [[film]] from the opposite side of an imaginary axis on set in order to view the actors from the opposite direction.

